{"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestPathTree"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ShortestPathTree.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree.swift#L29"},"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths0A8PathTreeV","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"title":"ShortestPathTree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"identifier"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Shortest paths from one or more sources: for each reached vertex, its distance, its parent and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the edge from the parent (a forest when there are several sources).","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/sources"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(checkedTo:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(toIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/hasPath(checkedTo:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/hasPath(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(checked:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(of:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parentEdge(checked:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parentEdge(of:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/path(checkedTo:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/path(to:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The first relaxation to a vertex’s final distance wins. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"parent(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest-path predecessor of ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" settled first. Vertices at equal distance settle in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified order, so when several vertices at the same smallest distance lead to ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" along","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest paths, which one is the parent is unspecified. Among parallel edges from the parent,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the parent edge is the cheapest, and the first in ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order among equals.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A tree holds a copy of the graph, so looking a vertex up never hashes on a representation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with cheap vertex indices. While the tree is alive, the next mutation of the original copies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it; a tree of a graph about to change should be read and dropped first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With several sources, each starts at distance zero (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".one"},{"text":" over a semiring) with no parent.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dijkstra’s algorithm and breadth-first search never improve on that, so a source keeps no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parent even when another source reaches it. Bellman–Ford treats the sources as one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"super-source: a negative path from one source to another improves the second, which then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has that distance, a parent and a path from the first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Over a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SelectiveSemiring"},{"type":"text","text":" a distance is the ⊗-product of a path’s weights, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"best by the natural order "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"type":"text","text":", and a vertex is reached exactly when its distance is not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".zero"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": two correct trees can choose different parents on ties.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestpathtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://ShortestPaths/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://ShortestPaths/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/ShortestPathTree/path(checkedTo:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"path(checkedTo:)","abstract":[{"code":"path(to: vertex)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", throwing instead of trapping when "},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not a vertex of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph: nil still means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" is not reached. O(length)."}],"role":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Distance"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"path"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"checkedTo